<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?><rss xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom" version="2.0"><channel><title>World News, Today World News, Latest International News, World Breaking News, Trending News of World - Times of India</title><link>https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world</link><description>World News Today: Read the latest world news headlines, Current International breaking news world wide. In depth analysis and top news headlines world wide.</description><language>en-gb</language><lastBuildDate>2026-10-06T14:31:07+05:30</lastBuildDate><atom:link type="application/rss+xml" rel="self" href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/rssfeeds/296589292.cms"/><copyright>Copyright:(C) Tue, 06 Oct 2026 14:31:07 IST Bennett Coleman &amp; Co. Ltd, http://in.indiatimes.com/policyterms/1554651.cms</copyright><docs>http://syndication.indiatimes.com/</docs><image><title>World News, Today World News, Latest International News, World Breaking News, Trending News of World - Times of India</title><url>https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/507610.cms</url><link>https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world</link></image><item><title><![CDATA[Florida woman rides 7,000 miles, raises $17,560 for charity that helped her two decades ago]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134727089.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[A Florida woman completed a 7,000-mile motorcycle journey across 48 states in six days. She raised $17,560 for Quantum House, an organization that supported her during her daughter’s hospital stay. The ride attracted attention, allowing her to create awareness about the organization. Jess's daughter, who benefitted from Quantum House, joined her when she presented the raised funds.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/a-florida-woman-rode-7000-miles-through-48-states-in-six-days-then-donated-17560-to-the-house-that-supported-her-when-her-2-pound-newborn-spent-nearly-three-months-in-intensive-care/articleshow/134727089.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/a-florida-woman-rode-7000-miles-through-48-states-in-six-days-then-donated-17560-to-the-house-that-supported-her-when-her-2-pound-newborn-spent-nearly-three-months-in-intensive-care/articleshow/134727089.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-06T14:30:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134729405,imgsize-143048.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[South African tycoon to spend $402M turning 600-hectare farm into F1 circuit by 2031]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134725482.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Neal Froneman leads a consortium aiming to construct a $402 million Formula 1 circuit near Cape Town, marking a potential revival of South African motorsport after nearly 40 years. Currently in the pre-feasibility phase, the circuit is designed to accommodate 125,000 fans and will include a media complex and entertainment spots. If the endeavor succeeds, it could generate over 15,000 local jobs, enhancing tourism and the economy.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/south-african-mining-tycoon-neal-froneman-to-spend-402-million-turning-a-600-hectare-farmland-into-a-formula-1-circuit-to-bring-racing-back-to-the-country-by-2031/articleshow/134725482.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/south-african-mining-tycoon-neal-froneman-to-spend-402-million-turning-a-600-hectare-farmland-into-a-formula-1-circuit-to-bring-racing-back-to-the-country-by-2031/articleshow/134725482.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-06T13:55:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134725876,imgsize-536055.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Ageing mice study finds why 'zombie cells' evade immune clearance and fuel inflammation]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134726224.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Researchers studying ageing in mice have found that a decline in chaperone-mediated autophagy (CMA), a cellular recycling process, helps “zombie cells” accumulate by weakening the immune system’s ability to clear them. Restoring CMA reduced senescent-cell buildup, inflammation and fibrosis in mice, pointing to a possible new approach to age-related diseases.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/discovery/researchers-studying-ageing-in-mice-found-that-declining-cellular-recycling-helps-zombie-cells-evade-immune-clearance-restoring-the-process-improved-their-removal-and-reduced-age-related-inflammation/articleshow/134726224.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/discovery/researchers-studying-ageing-in-mice-found-that-declining-cellular-recycling-helps-zombie-cells-evade-immune-clearance-restoring-the-process-improved-their-removal-and-reduced-age-related-inflammation/articleshow/134726224.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-06T13:30:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Science Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134727011,imgsize-52536.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[40 oyster reefs placed along Gandy's Beach in New Jersey to support live oysters and cut storm-wave]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134725091.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[A New Jersey project that began installing 40 constructed oyster reefs along about 800 metres of Gandy’s Beach in 2015 recorded more than 800 live oysters per square metre during early monitoring. Researchers also found the reefs reduced storm-wave height by up to 51% under certain conditions, though seven years of monitoring showed continued elevation and vegetation loss at the site.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/nature/in-2015-new-jersey-began-installing-40-oyster-reefs-along-about-800-metres-of-gandys-beach-the-structures-later-supported-more-than-800-live-oysters-per-square-metre-and-cut-storm-wave-height-by-up-to-51/articleshow/134725091.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/nature/in-2015-new-jersey-began-installing-40-oyster-reefs-along-about-800-metres-of-gandys-beach-the-structures-later-supported-more-than-800-live-oysters-per-square-metre-and-cut-storm-wave-height-by-up-to-51/articleshow/134725091.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-06T12:30:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Science Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134725831,imgsize-242838.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Golfer's $5 thrift-store jacket sells for $139,349]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134726443.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[A golfer made a surprising find in 1994 when he bought a striking green jacket for only $5 at a Toronto thrift shop. To his amazement, it turned out to be a genuine Augusta National club jacket dating back to the 1950s. By 2017, this piece of history sold for an impressive $139,349 at auction, illustrating the escalating demand and skyrocketing prices for rare golf collectibles in today’s marketplace.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/in-1994-a-golfer-paid-5-for-a-green-jacket-at-a-toronto-thrift-store-it-was-later-confirmed-as-an-authentic-1950s-augusta-national-club-jacket-and-it-sold-at-auction-in-2017-for-139349/articleshow/134726443.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/in-1994-a-golfer-paid-5-for-a-green-jacket-at-a-toronto-thrift-store-it-was-later-confirmed-as-an-authentic-1950s-augusta-national-club-jacket-and-it-sold-at-auction-in-2017-for-139349/articleshow/134726443.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-06T12:42:05+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134726581,imgsize-21898.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[North Dakota governor’s residence project uncovers seven coffins and human remains]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134726713.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/a-2-35-million-security-project-at-north-dakotas-governors-residence-uncovered-human-remains-archaeologists-have-now-removed-7-coffins-after-examining-more-than-80-areas-around-the-construction-site/articleshow/134726713.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/a-2-35-million-security-project-at-north-dakotas-governors-residence-uncovered-human-remains-archaeologists-have-now-removed-7-coffins-after-examining-more-than-80-areas-around-the-construction-site/articleshow/134726713.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-06T13:00:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134726752,imgsize-1489176.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Jeff McKissack built Houston’s Orange Show from salvaged materials in 1968]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;m