gin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134724366.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/southern-california-once-had-so-many-of-these-mountain-frogs-that-people-could-barely-avoid-stepping-on-them-now-about-650-were-released-back-into-the-wild/articleshow/134724366.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/southern-california-once-had-so-many-of-these-mountain-frogs-that-people-could-barely-avoid-stepping-on-them-now-about-650-were-released-back-into-the-wild/articleshow/134724366.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-06T11:16:14+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134724539,imgsize-1864957.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[219 box turtles rescued after hundreds were dumped near New Jersey river]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134723669.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[The Mercer County Wildlife Center is diligently working to rehabilitate 219 abandoned box turtles, found near Cranford, New Jersey, back in July. A significant rescue operation was launched after these turtles were discovered by the riverbank. With winter on the horizon, the center is building outdoor enclosures to allow the turtles to brumate naturally.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/a-new-jersey-wildlife-centre-is-caring-for-219-box-turtles-after-hundreds-were-dumped-near-a-river-rescuers-are-now-building-outdoor-enclosures-so-the-turtles-can-spend-winter-as-they-would-in-the-wild/articleshow/134723669.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/a-new-jersey-wildlife-centre-is-caring-for-219-box-turtles-after-hundreds-were-dumped-near-a-river-rescuers-are-now-building-outdoor-enclosures-so-the-turtles-can-spend-winter-as-they-would-in-the-wild/articleshow/134723669.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-06T11:13:37+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134723855,imgsize-127234.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Soldiers looking for land mines in South Korea have found the country's oldest gun dating back to more than 600 years]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134722534.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[In a fascinating search for hidden landmines, South Korean troops discovered a small bronze gun buried beneath the earth. Dubbed a Hwangja Hwatong, this artifact dates back to the 14th or 15th century. The intricate details engraved on it can help historians piece together Korea's journey in firearm technology and military tactics from the times of the Goryeo and early Joseon dynasties.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/archaeology/soldiers-looking-for-land-mines-in-south-korea-have-found-the-countrys-oldest-gun-a-600-year-old-inscribed-bronze-tube-used-to-fire-gunpowder-propelled-arrows/articleshow/134722534.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/archaeology/soldiers-looking-for-land-mines-in-south-korea-have-found-the-countrys-oldest-gun-a-600-year-old-inscribed-bronze-tube-used-to-fire-gunpowder-propelled-arrows/articleshow/134722534.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-06T11:00:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Science Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134722559,imgsize-544580.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[650 drones overnight: Ukraine unleashes massive strike on Moscow region]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="le